hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"19180","Waki narrated to us: Hisham ibn Sad informed us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ibn al-Adra, he said: I guarded the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) one night, and he went out for some need. He said: So he saw me and took my hand, and we went and passed a man praying loud with the Quran. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Perhaps he is showing off. He said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, he prays loud with the Quran. He said: So he released my hand, then said: You shall never attain this matter by rivalry. He said: Then he went out one night while I guarded him for some need, and he took my hand, and we passed a man praying with the Quran. He said: So I said: Perhaps he is showing off. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No, he is oft-returning. He said: So I looked, and there he was Abd Allah Dhu al-Bijadayn."
